# config/defconfigs/fleet.config — RISC-V 64 / Generic board / Fleet profile
#
# Target: Edge-gateway server — a single AZOS instance aggregating many
#         downstream robots.  Pure profile preset — heaviest sizing on rv64.
#         Intended for powerful SBCs or mini-PCs (x86_64 gateway also works;
#         swap ARCH to x86_64 and regenerate).
#
# Memory budget (measured 2026-09-14 on the riscv64 release ELF; tools/size_report.sh):
#   Static image: 140,517,202 B = 134 MiB, of which
#     MAX_TASKS=4096: kernel stacks 4096 × 32 KiB = 128 MiB, task slots 3.3 MiB
#       (32 KiB since 2026-09-16: the receive path overflowed 16 KiB and faulted)
#     TCP_MAX_CONNS=1024 × (2 × TCP_BUF_SIZE 16 KiB + 6,088 B) = 37.9 MiB  (RX+TX rings + state)
#     capability tables 8.0 MiB, per-CPU scheduler state 8.0 MiB, pipes 4.0 MiB
#   Kernel heap (KERNEL_HEAP_SIZE = 262144 KiB): 256 MiB, taken from the page allocator after the image
#   Lazy user stacks (MAX_TASKS=4096 × 16 KiB demand-paged): ~64 MiB virtual
#   Total worst-case: ~518 MiB  (requires >= 1 GiB RAM; gateway targets have 4+ GiB)
#
# RAM_SIZE is the page allocator's ceiling (crates/core/mm/src/pmm.rs MAX_PAGES), whatever the
# board has. The generic board's default of 256 MiB leaves no room for the heap after a
# 134 MiB image, and boot stops at "[MM] Heap FAILED:". 1024 MiB covers the budget above;
# a board with less RAM still boots the same image only if the budget fits in what it has.
#
# Notable vs. edge defaults:
#   ARCH=RISCV64, BOARD=GENERIC (configure UART_BASE/PLIC_BASE/RAM per gateway SoC).
#   PROFILE_FLEET — largest cap tier.
#   MAX_TASKS=4096, TCP_MAX_CONNS=1024, MAX_CAPS_TOTAL=65536, KERNEL_HEAP=256 MiB.
#   SCHED_HZ=500 (PROFILE_FLEET default — tighter preemption for many tasks).
#   DEFAULT_QUANTUM_US=5000 (PROFILE_FLEET default — shorter quantum).
#   DRV_VIRTIO_BLK_NET=n (auto from !BOARD_QEMU).
#   All other drivers enabled by default; disable unused ones per deployment.
#
# Used for: fleet gateway servers, multi-robot aggregation, CI fleet-profile build.
#
# Regenerate with:  make defconfig-fleet && make savedefconfig
# Domain (wave 11, DOMAIN): none set, so the Kconfig default, Generic: no
# robot crate is linked. config/defconfigs/robot-fleet.config is the same
# profile with DOMAIN_ROBOT (the robot worked example; the gate builds that).

CONFIG_BOARD_GENERIC=y
CONFIG_PROFILE_FLEET=y
CONFIG_RAM_SIZE=1024
